    "lawCode": "Add §52, UDC Act",
    "lawSection": "New York State Urban Development Corporation Act",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6536\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the New York state urban development\ncorporation act, in relation to the creation of the strategic\ninvestment in workforce development program\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo establish within the New York state urban development corporation,\nthe strategic investment in workforce development program to identify\nand address workforce needs throughout the state.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 amends Section 1 of chapter 174 of the laws of 1968 by\nadding a new section 52 which establishes the strategic workforce\ndevelopment program.\n\nSection 2 provides that the act will take effect immediately, and\nshall be deemed to have been in full force and effect on and after\nApril 1, 2017\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe strategic investment in workforce development program is needed to\ncollaborate with the department of labor, the department of economic\ndevelopment, the state university of New York, the city university of\nNew York, and the state education department to better collect and\nutilize information to target workforce training activities and to\nprovide resources for training and skills development activities for\nunemployed or underemployed youth. Eligible applicants shall include,\nbut not be limited to, not-for-profits, educational entities, or\nprograms that provide training and skill development.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
